# What `docker compose build` may send to Docker (the build context is the repo root).
#
# An allowlist: ignore everything, then let in only the three folders the image uses.
# That keeps out .git, .venv, .env, design-ref/, CLAUDE.md, PROJECT.md,
# BACKEND-GUIDE.md, FRONTEND-HANDOFF.md and any other local notes, including
# ones added later that nobody remembers to list here.
*
!server
!agent
!deploy

# Inside those folders: no tests, fixtures, local data, secrets, caches or notes.
**/tests
**/fixtures
server/data
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.sqlite3-*
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.md

# No npm files: the image has no Node, so these could only ever be stray files. They must
# stay below the ! lines above, because the last matching rule wins.
**/node_modules
**/package*.json
**/yarn.lock
**/pnpm-lock.yaml
